#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:102
msgid ""
"Changes are grouped by impact in that order. If you just want to port your "
"code, jump to the :ref:`migration checklist <v3_6_1_migration>` at the end. "
"Each commit hash links to its diff on GitHub."
msgstr ""
"Les changements sont regroupés par impact dans cet ordre. Si vous souhaitez "
"simplement porter votre code, passez à la :ref:`liste de contrôle de "
"migration <v3_6_1_migration>` à la fin. Chaque hash de commit renvoie vers "
"son diff sur GitHub."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:109
msgid ":func:`sensor.set_framerate` removed *(minor)*"
msgstr ":func:`sensor.set_framerate` supprimé *(minor)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:111
msgid ""
"The no-op :func:`sensor.set_framerate` stub was removed; calling it now "
"raises ``AttributeError``. Remove the call and control frame timing via "
"framesize/exposure instead. (A working ``set_framerate()`` is re-introduced "
"in v4.0.2.)"
msgstr ""
"Le stub sans effet :func:`sensor.set_framerate` a été supprimé ; l'appeler "
"lève désormais ``AttributeError``. Supprimez l'appel et contrôlez la cadence"
" des trames via la framesize/l'exposition à la place. (Un "
"``set_framerate()`` fonctionnel est réintroduit dans la v4.0.2.)"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:116
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `705e98f91 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/705e98f91>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits :* `705e98f91 "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/705e98f91>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:121
msgid "TensorFlow dropped on the OpenMV Cam M7 *(minor)*"
msgstr "TensorFlow abandonné sur l'OpenMV Cam M7 *(minor)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:123
msgid ""
"TensorFlow (the ``tf`` module) was disabled on the OpenMV Cam M7 / OpenMV 3 "
"(it no longer fits). ``import tf`` on the M7 fails — use an H7-class camera "
"for TensorFlow. (``tf`` is re-enabled on the F7 in v3.6.3.)"
msgstr ""
"TensorFlow (le module ``tf``) a été désactivé sur l'OpenMV Cam M7 / OpenMV 3"
" (il n'y tient plus). ``import tf`` échoue sur le M7 — utilisez une caméra "
"de classe H7 pour TensorFlow. (``tf`` est réactivé sur le F7 dans la "
"v3.6.3.)"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:127
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `2ae875077 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/2ae875077>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits :* `2ae875077 "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/2ae875077>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:132
msgid "``set_pixformat()`` / ``set_framesize()`` return ``None`` *(behavior)*"
msgstr ""
"``set_pixformat()`` / ``set_framesize()`` renvoient ``None`` *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:134
msgid ""
":func:`sensor.set_pixformat` and :func:`sensor.set_framesize` now return "
"``None`` instead of ``True``, and an unsupported pixel format now raises a "
"``ValueError`` instead of an assertion. Code that checked the return value "
"(e.g. ``if sensor.set_pixformat(...):``) must stop doing so, and code that "
"caught ``AssertionError`` for unsupported formats must catch ``ValueError``."
msgstr ""
":func:`sensor.set_pixformat` et :func:`sensor.set_framesize` renvoient "
"désormais ``None`` au lieu de ``True``, et un format de pixel non pris en "
"charge lève désormais une ``ValueError`` au lieu d'une assertion. Le code "
"qui vérifiait la valeur de retour (par ex. ``if "
"sensor.set_pixformat(...):``) doit cesser de le faire, et le code qui "
"interceptait ``AssertionError`` pour les formats non pris en charge doit "
"intercepter ``ValueError``."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:140
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `f314ac4e7 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/f314ac4e7>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits :* `f314ac4e7 "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/f314ac4e7>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:145
msgid ""
"``lens_corr()`` / ``linpolar()`` / ``logpolar()`` require even dimensions "
"*(behavior)*"
msgstr ""
"``lens_corr()`` / ``linpolar()`` / ``logpolar()`` exigent des dimensions "
"paires *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:147
msgid ""
"``image.lens_corr()`` and ``image.linpolar()`` / ``image.logpolar()`` now "
"require even image width and height and raise an error on odd dimensions. "
"Crop or resize the image to even dimensions before calling these methods."
msgstr ""
"``image.lens_corr()`` et ``image.linpolar()`` / ``image.logpolar()`` exigent"
" désormais une largeur et une hauteur d'image paires et lèvent une erreur "
"sur des dimensions impaires. Recadrez ou redimensionnez l'image en "
"dimensions paires avant d'appeler ces méthodes."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.6.1.rst:151
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `b36460a36 "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/b36460a36>`__, `2b26ca17b "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/2b26ca17b>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits :* `b36460a36 "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/b36460a36>`__, `2b26ca17b "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/2b26ca17b>`__"

